// **the flip weak references rest on.** a class handle used to accept `null` whether or not its author wanted
// one, so nothing could be relied on to hold an object. now a bare `Foo` is a promise that there is one,
// and `Foo?` is how you say there may not be
//
// the same rule reaches every type, which is what makes it one rule rather than a class special case

class Node { int32 $tag; }

Node $mustBeThere = null;

int32 $alsoNot = null;
